desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Force Ssl False"
	title_zh: "Force Ssl False"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-force-ssl-false"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `force-ssl-false` (ruby/lang/security/force-ssl-false.yaml).
Original message: Checks for configuration setting of force_ssl to false. Force_ssl forces usage of HTTPS, which could lead to network interception of unencrypted application traffic. To fix, set config.force_ssl = true.
CWE: CWE-311: Missing Encryption of Sensitive Data
References:
- https://github.com/presidentbeef/brakeman/blob/main/lib/brakeman/checks/check_force_ssl.rb
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Preferred replacement: = true
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.rb": <<<POS
config.force_ssl = false
POS
	"safefile://pos.rb": <<<NEG
config.force_ssl = true
NEG
)

${*.rb}.pattern_regex(/(?:config\.force_ssl\s+=\s+false)/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Force Ssl False",
	title_zh: "Force Ssl False",
	message: "Force Ssl False detected.",
}
